  "discovery": {
    "//": "TE15 R7.1.3 discovery-tree parity. Each leg materializes the same tree into its own sandbox user-agent dir: upstream substitutes `<CFGDIR>` with `.pi`, rpi with `.rpi`, and both normalize the config-dir segment back to `<CFGDIR>`. `linked-nested`/`cycle` symlinks are created on both legs on non-Windows platforms only (materialize.json records the same limitation). Scope is `user` on both sides so builtin catalogs do not participate.",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "user-tree-robustness",
        "tree": {
          "files": {
            "good.md": "---\nname: good-agent\ndescription: Valid fixture agent used by the discovery parity tree (R7.1.3, TE15).\ntools: read, bash\n---\n\nYou are a valid fixture agent. Reply with the requested text only.\n",
            "nested/good-nested.md": "---\nname: good-nested\ndescription: Valid nested fixture agent (recursive discovery).\ntools: read\n---\n\nNested fixture body.\n",
            "broken-frontmatter.md": "---\nname: broken-unterminated\ndescription: Frontmatter never closes (R7.1.3.1 malformed-definition fixture).\n\nBody without a closing delimiter.\n",
            "broken-no-colon.md": "---\nname: broken-no-colon\nthis line has no colon\ntools: read\n---\n\nBody after a malformed frontmatter line.\n",
            "broken-invalid-async.md": "---\nname: broken-async\ndescription: Fatal frontmatter (invalid async) - discovery must isolate it (R7.1.3.1 #1200).\nasync: maybe\ntools: read\n---\n\nThis file exists only to produce one discovery diagnostic.\n",
            "broken-invalid-timeout.md": "---\nname: broken-timeout\ndescription: Fatal frontmatter (invalid timeoutMs) - discovery must isolate it (R7.1.3.1 #1200).\ntimeoutMs: not-a-number\ntools: read\n---\n\nThis file exists only to produce one discovery diagnostic.\n",
            "sync-backups/pruned.md": "---\nname: sync-backup-agent\ndescription: Must be pruned by discovery (R7.1.3.2 `sync-backups`).\ntools: read\n---\n\nThis file exists only to prove the `sync-backups` directory is pruned.\n",
            "<CFGDIR>/pruned.md": "---\nname: hidden-rpi-agent\ndescription: Must be pruned by discovery (R7.1.3.2 `.rpi`).\ntools: read\n---\n\nThis file exists only to prove the `.rpi` directory is pruned.\n"
          },
          "symlinks": [
            {
              "path": "linked-nested",
              "target": "nested"
            },
            {
              "path": "cycle",
              "target": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "notify": {
    "//": "TE17 (R7.1.7.2) completion-notice cases. `format` feeds the upstream-shaped details to formatSingleCompletion on both legs; the Rust leg maps childRuns[0].runId to its single-run run_id. The `Saved output:` line is an rpi-only addition (upstream carries saved paths inside childOutputs blocks / preview text) and therefore NOT part of the byte-comparable slice - it is covered by crate unit tests. `parse` cases assert the shared parse projection (runId from childRuns[0]).",
    "cases": [
      {
        "name": "single-basic",
        "kind": "format",
        "details": {
          "agent": "scout",
          "status": "completed",
          "resultPreview": "all mapped",
          "sessionLabel": "Session file",
          "sessionValue": "/home/user/sessions/abc.jsonl"
